english":"Each of the terrific and mightiest councillors of the Rākşasa-chief, coped with a thousand Yaksas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.475,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6cc4a6c3b81fd574565f57f649bc922c2210c4b2fa7ce6d0c8ff99b56f0ae589","compact":"befd972a678db1ee743835dc2c1d61d15cdbe313e9cd9b3b682c27de0c7dda09","nasal":"eba438e2f956e3a5db04d38b996411abe0c74850bbde4790a02e5aba8c08254d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":10,"english":"And then struck with maces and clubs and swords and darts and tomaras, the Ten-necked one dived into (that deep) of a host. And rendered inert and sore assailed, Daśānana was deprived of his movements with volleys of weapons resembling torrents of rain. And albeit drenched with blood streaming dowli in hundreds of torrents, he like a mountain flooded with a downpour, being wounded with the weapons of the Yakşa, does not betray any smart.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.554,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a13288032d8a278c0281dad486206e51e93c6a08aa66acbe1509974493248e5a","compact":"a5852d458651d26d73a9760a9d1bb788b40ca9084ed5bd71d545445cfd6a5dc9","nasal":"a5852d458651d26d73a9760a9d1bb788b40ca9084ed5bd71d545445cfd6a5dc9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":11,"english":"And then struck with maces and clubs and swords and darts and tomaras, the Ten-necked one dived into (that deep) of a host. And rendered inert and sore assailed, Daśānana was deprived of his movements with volleys of weapons resembling torrents of rain. And albeit drenched with blood streaming dowli in hundreds of torrents, he like a mountain flooded with a downpour, being wounded with the weapons of the Yakşa, does not betray any smart.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.448,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ed4857cf7ebe2882816890bcc0541f7a9af46e4994670e0b032a2aa3ea2c7b5","compact":"6e382e6cb304a57342126c40de186e2191374e99f6aa7e0d0c603daed076b2aa","nasal":"a6234f9f09ddf0c5377a6b4ab885e0c56f4597186f22f974e353695d7419759e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":12,"english":"And that high-souled one, raising up his mace resembling the rod itself of Time, entered into that army, despatching Yakşas to the abode of Yama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.812,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"852797ab385719c29145f8f5df0d160b27bbc44f564d29cc481180b094a0555a","compact":"2088f4ac10b3acf34290fd771c4e86e3cc11422c39772eb6404401c9e410c6a9","nasal":"4566f9f3445713b3dc154828e8a7d7d92e10e32164aeeebfac5a5411512ef9e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":13,"english":"And as a flaming fire burn up an extensive sward of grass stocked with dry fire-wood, he began to consume that Yakşa army.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e009ce4ddc920c13f1cb0f87bd5059c1fc946af1f6ae8800b4730058a5275d04","compact":"5ce320590f838ae30971b3185f003661cef07458b35970a949d69630ac30eecf","nasal":"5f0e00042e81118e1bf05d336c500ba6fea4fb7540796a6a731d47175f6eeb23"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":14,"english":"And as the wind scatter clouds, the small remnant of Yaksa army was scattered by the redoubtable councillors (of Ravana) Mahodara, Suka, etc.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf56766944c81affb0a2788433da3b2aa23b9cac2d1b3bcda4db65d9186005d8","compact":"d6be3d2debec6be2f4571295ad8da750945299009ee414990e5fe015856d4a55","nasal":"c01f69ebbef9861da887aa2d347d393c793792c294457a994042fb3829a1acaf"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":15,"english":"And some were wounded, and (some) broken down, and (some) measured their lengths on the ground in the encounter, and other Yakşas deprived of their arms in the field, being fatigued, sank down, embracing each other, even as banks drop down, on being worn away by water.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.213,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9797433c3bda213b68e7cd7dd3398d3914e526655d981285c7f60cc756670066","compact":"bde34373f5aea89dea9bfe31bb6607f8c520b9c702c403d5947bfcc8bc8d493d","nasal":"41fb46f4a7e4a8da558f3f67bec6d33eb53e8a7501a2e3b2420919e79a2e4930"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":16,"english":"And some were wounded, and (some) broken down, and (some) measured their lengths on the ground in the encounter, and other Yakşas deprived of their arms in the field, being fatigued, sank down, embracing each other, even as banks drop down, on being worn away by water.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.429,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ef556dfaf437d937c0d655a0100158dd292f5e1b862af9f3dbbbbacf3d14c18","compact":"964263160461d2a1e6705b29528740e92a1f0a483022c4e8ff6dcbc5e770c1f2","nasal":"832f67dbb72b668be236fae096f5a69d6c8fe8b0394fba71c87449669d9a4d9e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":17,"english":"And no room was left (in the sky) in consequence of its being thronged by hosts of sages; and warriors, wounded and rushing for conflict, and (finally) ascending heaven.* *The idea of the author is: \"The welkin was thronged with sages as well as warriors, who swelled the ranks of the sages stationed in the sky, by ascending heaven after having fallen in fight.”","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.121,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"57ba98ce454311fbb668600071240f56761f80934163fca21ed177548a53a42a","compact":"9b5680a3cfe4377e0085732f5ef75cee15c19577e3ee19c44833fa261ace3c4a","nasal":"9bf4a75463250101da9db1bc198676ca41ae501d2e721dc997e97390c812410b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-14-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":14,"verse":18,"english":"In the meantime, o Rāma, a Yakşa named Sañyodhakanțaka, accompanied by an extensive force and a large number of vehicles, on being despatched, rushed (on the foe).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-14-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7014018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c40201a6de4108599ffe0b3c600aaa522487fd60d46ee704b6daf77647dd191","compact":"218490ac4c1e057ab212